! Similar Tiddlers

The Similar Tiddlers widget uses witness fingerprint analysis to find tiddlers that are semantically similar to the current one.

---

!! Usage

```
<$similar-tiddlers tiddler={{!!title}} threshold="0.3" max="5"/>
```

---

!! Parameters

* ''tiddler'' - The target tiddler to find similarities for (defaults to current tiddler)
* ''threshold'' - Similarity threshold 0-1, where lower values require more similarity (default: 0.3)
* ''max'' - Maximum number of results to display (default: 10)

---

!! How It Works

The witness fingerprint system analyzes several aspects of each tiddler:

* ''Phase'' - Semantic direction based on content
* ''Depth'' - Position in the tag hierarchy
* ''Sector'' - Domain classification from tags
* ''Monodromy'' - Cyclic reference patterns
* ''Link Density'' - Ratio of links to content
* ''Transclusion Complexity'' - Number of transclusions and macros
* ''Field Complexity'' - Number of custom fields

These dimensions are combined to create a unique fingerprint for each tiddler, allowing semantic similarity detection beyond simple keyword matching.

---

!! Example

Try it on this tiddler:

<$similar-tiddlers tiddler={{!!title}} threshold="0.4" max="5"/>

---

!! Technical Details

Based on the CE Tower witness operator from antclock research:
https://github.com/selfapplied/antclock/blob/main/arXiv/working.md

The witness operator <>g extracts self-describing invariant signatures as multi-dimensional fingerprints, enabling compositional analysis and resonance detection.
